          "title": "Latent variable joint model",
          "mustKnow": "Know how hidden variables make a model expressive.",
          "coreIdea": "A latent variable model defines a joint distribution over observations and hidden variables, so hidden structure can explain clusters, styles, causes, or low-dimensional factors.",
          "formulaOrRule": "Specify a prior over z and a conditional likelihood for x given z.",
          "formula": "p_\\theta(x,z)=p_\\theta(x|z)p(z)",
          "formulaHtml": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>",
