              "points": "1.0p",
              "type": "mechanism",
              "prompt": "What is the problem when training with the score-matching loss?",
              "promptHtml": "<p>What is the problem when training with the score-matching loss?</p>",
              "answer": "Classical score matching can require expensive derivatives of the score network, such as divergence or trace of a Jacobian. It can also be ill-behaved near data manifolds where the empirical data distribution has little support.",
              "answerHtml": "<p>Classical score matching can require expensive derivatives of the score network, such as divergence or trace of a Jacobian. It can also be ill-behaved near data manifolds where the empirical data distribution has little support.</p>",
              "explanation": "This motivates denoising score matching and noise levels.",
