              "promptHtml": "<p>Which statements are true about the transformer architecture? Select all that apply.</p>\n<ul><li>The decoder uses masked self-attention to prevent attending to future positions during training.</li><li>The Transformer encoder consists of stacked layers, each containing a multi-head self-attention sublayer followed by a feedforward sublayer.</li><li>Transformer models have a fixed-length context window determined by the number of layers in the network.</li><li>A Transformer model must always include both an encoder and a decoder.</li><li>Residual connections are used in Transformer layers to help stabilize training and mitigate vanishing gradients.</li></ul>",
