        "front": "Example 2e (Energy-based models): What is the log-likelihood $\\log p_\\theta(x)$?",
        "answer": "\\log p_\\theta(x)=-E_\\theta(x)-\\log Z_\\theta.",
        "answerHtml": "<div class=\"math-block\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Display formula\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub><mo>&#x0002E;</mo></mrow></math></div>",
        "explanation": "Take the log of the exponential numerator divided by $Z_\\theta$.",
