        "front": "Example 2g (Energy-based models): Briefly describe what the two terms in the EBM likelihood gradient are doing to the energy function qualitatively.",
        "answer": "Under gradient ascent, the data term lowers energy on observed data. The model-expectation term raises energy on samples from the current model distribution, often called negative samples. This creates the positive-phase / negative-phase push-pull.",
        "answerHtml": "<p>Under gradient ascent, the data term lowers energy on observed data. The model-expectation term raises energy on samples from the current model distribution, often called negative samples. This creates the positive-phase / negative-phase push-pull.</p>",
        "explanation": "A good answer uses energy language, not only probability language.",
