        "answerHtml": "<p>The numerator is non-negative if parameterized by an exponential or positive function, and dividing by <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><msub><mover><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007E;</mo></mover><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math></span> makes the total probability integrate to one, assuming <span class=\"inline-math\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></msub></mrow></math></span> is finite.</p>",
